DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T193000
UID:aeccf33a25a8f07c525bd0e11ff06517@growthzone.com
DESCRIPTION:First contacted by the Western world in the 1960’s\, the Ach
 uar people of the Ecuadorian Amazon have spent the intervening decades pro
 tecting the rainforest from oil drilling\, gold mining\, and logging. The 
 Achuar recognize themselves to be the forest and understand that the prote
 ction of the jungle\, their culture and their communities are inseparable.
  Come spend an evening with Achuar guide and leader of his community\, Ram
 iro Vargas\, lovingly known as Chumpi\, in conversation about the Achuar w
 ay of life and what it is to live at one with nature. Chumpi will speak ab
 out how\, despite increasing threats of environmental destruction and cult
 ural imperialism\, they are nurturing and sustaining their language\, life
 ways\, and traditions. Community cohesion and capacity for intergeneration
 al exchange are critical for the protection of territory\, traditional kno
 wledge and rights. Chumpi will share the simple but innovative ways of fos
 tering unity in the Achuar territories. All are
URL:https://business.sebastopol.org/events/details/an-evening-with-amazoni
 an-leader-ramiro-vargas
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
